course: dictionary
lesson: 4146
title: Glow: light, warmth and feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Glow has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one you need. «Then Mum saw the glow under her door.» There is no fire in that sentence, so glow means a soft light, and the clue is that Mum could see it.
explain: «The tiger is not on fire: its orange stripes seem to glow like flames in the dark forest.» The words not on fire warn you that glow does not mean burning. It means shining softly, so the stripes look bright and powerful.
explain: Glow can also describe a face. After a race, someone's cheeks glow, which means they look warm, pink and healthy. Ask: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: To glow is to give out a soft, steady light without flames.
fact: A glow is a soft, warm light, as in «a warm glow» or «the glow of the fire».
fact: To glow can mean to look warm, pink or healthy, often after exercise or when happy.
fact: To glow with a feeling means to show it clearly, as in «glowing with pride».
fact: Some things glow because they are hot, like embers; glow-in-the-dark toys store light and give it back slowly.
exercise: «Then Mum saw the glow under her door.» What is the glow? | *A soft light | A loud bang | A cold draught | A pile of washing
exercise: «The tiger is not on fire: its orange stripes seem to glow like flames in the dark forest.» Why does the author say not on fire? | To say the forest is safe | To show the tiger is hot and angry | To explain the tiger has no stripes | *To warn that glow means shining, not burning
exercise: After a race, Ayesha's cheeks glow. What does glow mean here? | Give out a bright white light | Feel cold and wet | Burn with flames | *Look warm, pink and healthy
test: Nadia says, «He was glowing with pride.» What does glowing with pride mean? | Feeling sorry for himself | *Showing his pride clearly | Hiding his pride | Shining like a torch
test: In «a warm glow», what kind of word is glow? | An adjective | *A noun | A verb | A question word
exam: Which sentence uses glow to mean showing a feeling clearly? | The tiger's stripes glow in the dark forest. | The lamp will glow softly all night. | *She glowed with pride when her picture won. | The bus will glow when it turns left.
